WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<i>He went for an ace again!</i>

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.030
30-love.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.990
All right, Yosshi! That's it!

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.520
<i>My reaction was good that time, too.</i>

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.770
<i>Ide-kun's aim is just too tight.</i>

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.630
<i>The shots that just missed going in before</i>

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.140
<i>are going in now.</i>

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.460
<i>Don't panic. I'm always at a 
disadvantage in my return game.</i>

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.500
<i>I'm doing what I need to do.</i>

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.260
<i>Now he's moving up!</i>

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.940
40-love.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.790
Okay, get one more point and hold serve!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.710
Game: Ide. Score: 4-1.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.800
Maruo leads.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.280
All right! Now he's gonna 
show his true strength!

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.250
Yes!

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.030
Show us a dramatic comeback!

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.440
Way to hold serve, Yosshi!

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.580
Now you're looking more like our Yosshi!

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.800
It's getting interesting now!

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.460
All right!

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.500
<i>Looking at my notes will help me 
remember past points more clearly.</i>

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.850
<i>But first, I should record the newest data.</i>

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.750
<i>Everything's okay up to this point.</i>

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.890
<i>He was able to hold serve this time,</i>

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.980
<i>but my reactions have improved.</i>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.380
<i>With more data, I should be able 
to understand him even better.</i>

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.840
<i>This isn't the only data I have on Ide-kun.</i>

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.090
Whoa, check out what's in his racket bag.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:24.600
<i>This is from last year's All-Japan Junior 
Kanto Region Indoor Invitational.</i>

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.150
<i>This is from the tournament in winter,</i>

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.600
<i>and this is from STC's video of 
this year's prefectural qualifier.</i>

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.300
<i>These diagrams illustrate Ide-kun's tennis itself.</i>

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.170
<i>He's an unpredictable and intuitive player 
who doesn't have a definitive style.</i>

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.110
<i>I can see that quality of him clearly.</i>

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.080
Dramatic By Nature

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.090
Maruo-kun.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.210
Yes?

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.340
The allotted time has passed.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.910
I'm giving you a warning, too.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.650
Huh?! Wh-What about the call?

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:05.990
I gave the call.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.780
Oh! So you did!

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.600
What is with the two of you?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.280
<i>Huh... I thought he was 
totally different from me,</i>

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.730
<i>but I guess we're alike in some ways.</i>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.880
<i>That was close...</i>

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.480
<i>But it's good that I was 
able to use every second.</i>

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.610
<i>I have to hold serve here to win the first set!</i>

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.410
<i>Visualize my data on Ide-kun 
until the moment play begins,</i>

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.140
<i>and as soon as it does...</i>

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.880
<i>Focus on the Ide-kun in front of me!</i>

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.340
<i>It's coming down the line!</i>

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:43.710
Yes!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:44.680
15-love.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.600
<i>That return should've made it. That's weird.</i>

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.170
<i>Even when I hit a good shot,</i>

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.410
<i>Ide-kun aims down the line without 
consideration for any risk.</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:02.250
<i>I've visualized that data many times, 
so the image was still in my mind.</i>

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.860
<i>It's paying off!</i>

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.550
<i>Next, I'll go with a flat serve.</i>

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:10.620
<i>Ide-kun isn't consistent, so there's 
no telling how he'll return it.</i>

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.420
<i>But if I narrow down my predictions based 
on my image, and react accordingly...</i>

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.000
<i>I can get to where the ball is faster!</i>

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.410
Yes!

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.500
30-love.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>Again? What the heck?</i>

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:29.770
40-love.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.360
<i>I get it.</i>

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.520
<i>He's starting to move faster?</i>

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.020
<i>He was looking at his notes. 
That's all it took?</i>

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.560
<i>And more importantly, I'm in trouble here.</i>

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:42.960
Yes!

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.400
Game: Maruo. Score: 5-1.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.990
Maruo held serve again!

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.120
All right! Nice, nice!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.870
<i>I barely managed to hold 
on to my service advantage.</i>

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.790
<i>But that doesn't mean I 
can afford to relax yet.</i>

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.300
That's it!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.530
Game: Ide. Score: 5-2.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.720
Maruo leads.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.880
Yes!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.020
All right, Ide! You're able to hold serve now!

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.850
You're finally stepping up your game!

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.760
Now turn it around the way you always do!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.770
<i>I'm just barely holding my service games,</i>

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.530
<i>but he held his so easily.</i>

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.270
<i>If he breaks my serve, the whole 
flow of the match will change.</i>

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.040
<i>In any case, I need to drill as 
much data as I can into my head</i>

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.280
<i>and hold my next serve.</i>

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:31.530
<i>I have to take control of the first set 
before it becomes a close match!</i>

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.290
<i>Damn!</i>

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.400
<i>When he gets a faster start, 
his timing gets faster too,</i>

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.140
<i>so I have to adjust my timing again.</i>

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:41.540
<i>Let's see, what was it again?</i>

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.550
If he goes "bam" with a flat shot, 
I'll have to hit a "ta-tat."

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.220
Yosshi's opponent is pretty unique, too.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.300
Yeah.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.080
These two are a pretty interesting match-up.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:57.810
Yeah.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:58.870
Time.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.240
Um, hey, Yosshi?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.070
Ei-chan?

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.010
He has to break serve this game.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.660
Yeah, since it's 5-2.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.330
If he doesn't, he'll lose the first set.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.950
Yosshi will pull it off.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:16.580
Yeah.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.100
Yes!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.100
15-love.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.910
There's still time!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:26.590
Yeah!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:30.730
<i>Looks like his defensive range has widened 
by about one step to either side,</i>

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:35.350
<i>and his shots are just a hair faster overall.</i>

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.350
<i>Then I'll just have to go for a...</i>

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.260
"Da"!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.190
30-all.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.500
<i>No matter what I do, he adapts right away!</i>

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.650
<i>What in the world is this guy?</i>

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.860
Bam, tata... Bam, tata...

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.700
<i>I'll surprise him with a serve-and-volley!</i>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.740
40-30.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.450
Whoa! Maruo's at set point!

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.540
<i>If I don't win the set on this 
next point, I'm in trouble!</i>

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.490
<i>It really sucks when he gets a good serve in.</i>

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.790
<i>Wonder if I can at least guess 
which shot he'll use...</i>

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.900
<i>Before he can adapt...</i>

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:11.300
<i>Before this becomes a situation ideal for 
a guy who excels at close matches...</i>

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.970
<i>I have to finish it with this point!</i>

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.060
<i>Perfect first shot!</i>

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.260
<i>A rising shot down the line?!</i>

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.540
First set winner: Maruo.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.250
Score: 6-2.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.710
Whoa, incredible!

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.240
How wild was that rally?!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.910
All right! Ei-chan won the first set!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:36.490
Yeah!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.090
Oh, man...

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.990
He's just getting started!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.650
<i>Yes! I held on!</i>

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.580
<i>I'm past the first barrier!</i>

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:49.030
You're kidding! An unseeded 
player won the first set?!

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.230
No, he's really incredible, though!

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.340
Yeah, he stopped Ide from gaining momentum.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:58.350
<i>I thought I finally had the hang 
of it when we were at 0-4.</i>

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:01.160
<i>Since he broke out his notes,</i>

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.850
<i>he's been getting started faster, 
and it's harder to grasp the timing.</i>

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.660
<i>He was within range, but I couldn't catch up.</i>

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.490
<i>Is it even possible for someone's play 
to improve so much in one match?</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.360
<i>No...</i>

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.870
<i>He also made huge improvements during 
his match with Nabae, didn't he?</i>

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.090
All right! One more set and he wins!

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.230
Even if he's at a loss,

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:38.470
the fact that he's playing his own 
tennis makes a big difference.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.800
Everything he's done is working in his favor.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:44.640
In particular, it's a good 
thing I had him play Natsu.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:45.690
Huh?

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:46.890
He played Nat-chan?

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.720
It proved to him

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.000
that intuitive types aren't impossible 
for a logical type like him to beat.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.570
<i>This is where it really gets hard.</i>

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.080
<i>He keeps picking up on my timing,</i>

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:04.660
<i>so in the end, it's been all I could do 
to hold serve, let alone break.</i>

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.520
<i>I should put even more data 
on Ide-kun into my head,</i>

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.240
<i>and work on getting an even faster start.</i>

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.250
<i>And if he grasps my pace after I change it up,</i>

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.360
<i>I'll drop that pattern</i>

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.930
<i>and keep trying new patterns until I win.</i>

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.330
<i>I don't even have one notebook full 
of patterns I'm confident in,</i>

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.680
<i>but theoretically, the 
possibilities are infinite.</i>

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.190
Maruo Eiichiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:27.650
Time.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.230
<i>I won the first set,</i>

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.440
<i>so I'll keep trying more new 
patterns in the second.</i>

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.200
<i>That's fast!</i>

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:45.010
<i>If my serve is good, it limits the 
shots he can use to change the pace.</i>

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>I can keep it up!</i>

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.220
15-love.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:50.970
All right! Nice shot!

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.710
Make it happen!

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:56.960
<i>And I don't dislike being down a 
set going into the second one.</i>

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.900
<i>Everyone'll cheer their hearts out 
for me when I'm up against the wall!</i>

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.270
Yes!

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:05.470
30-love.

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:09.730
<i>So if I win points, everyone'll be thrilled for me!</i>

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.530
Yosshi, nice serve!

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.730
All right!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.700
<i>Fun times like these don't happen every day!</i>

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.650
Game: Ide. Score: 1-0.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:23.910
Second set.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.930
Way to hold serve, Ide!

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.540
Now break his serve next!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.540
Time to turn this thing around!

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:32.490
It'll be so awesome if he 
really does come back to win.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.040
You kind of start to expect 
that from Ide-kun, huh?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.510
I don't like the air around here.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.430
<i>Input all my new data every 
time we change sides,</i>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:49.800
<i>and once play begins...</i>

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.020
<i>Focus on my opponent!</i>

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:56.160
<i>If I can take the advantage on my serve,</i>

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:59.030
<i>I can change the pace and hit 
it to the ideal position.</i>

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.390
<i>And when he loses his balance,</i>

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:05.530
<i>hit it into the open space 
with my 1/64 control!</i>

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.030
15-love.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.100
Yes!

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.620
Wow, that Maruo kid really is good.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.420
He has incredible control.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.590
<i>This short crosscourt shot gets...</i>

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.090
"Da"!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.340
Yeah!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.340
15-all.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.090
All right! Take the lead, Ide!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.160
You've even got the edge 
in your return game!

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:31.100
Wh-What is this? All he did 
was win a point, too.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.070
<i>Focus!</i>

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:51.620
Maruo Eiichiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.520
Game: Maruo. 2-all.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.620
Second set.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.190
The second set...

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.620
Ei-chan can't break serve,

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.110
and he's barely even holding his own serves.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.370
Yeah!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.160
Game: Ide. 3-2.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.880
Ide leads. Second set.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.250
That's it, Ide!

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.350
Now break his serve!

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.010
<i>I'm being aggressive, and I've 
been able to change the pace.</i>

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.900
<i>So how does he keep pushing me like this?</i>

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:19.080
Yes!

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:20.810
Game: Ide. 4-3.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.650
Ide leads. Second set.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.020
Neither one's giving in. 
It's down to who can hold serve.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.410
But Ide's the one playing better tennis.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:31.490
<i>All the data is in my head,</i>

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.460
<i>and I'm concentrating on my opponent...</i>

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.620
<i>So why?</i>

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:41.670
<i>I've got his timing down, but I can't take 
that one last step to break his serve.</i>

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.670
Onii-chan!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.720
"Onii-chan"? Who's that?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.210
What? What's going on?

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:52.710
Oh!

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:53.930
Huh?

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:59.240
I got through the surgery like I promised!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.260
So...

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:04.030
So you have to win!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:09.700
Hey, that's not the kid who was in the 
accident before the match, is it?

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.780
The one Yosshi was taking care 
of that made him get here late.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.560
What? That's him?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.690
It is! He's in a wheelchair, 
and a nurse is with him!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.610
We're going back as soon as it's over, okay?

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:24.300
I'm sorry he asked to do this.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:27.360
Hey, I'm a friend of his.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.580
What did you two promise?

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:32.250
Huh? Oh, I said I didn't want surgery,

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:36.550
and he said he'd win his match, 
so I had to get through my surgery.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:39.810
Oh, did he? That's just like Yosshi.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:43.510
Hey, he promised he'd win for 
the kid from the accident!

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:46.070
This is just like a TV drama! Incredible!

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:51.720
<i>He came in a wheelchair?</i>

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:54.200
Time.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.150
Ide! Now you can't lose!

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:58.720
It's really getting exciting now!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.530
Come on, Ide!

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.370
<i>I'm already losing. This is bad.</i>

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.470
<i>I can't do anything dumb again.</i>

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:13.240
The air is starting to feel 
even worse around here.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:16.400
<i>Just as Okada-kun said,</i>

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.600
<i>it's like a TV drama is building 
itself around Ide-kun.</i>

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.510
<i>But I'm glad the boy who was hurt is okay.</i>

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.640
<i>I understand why everyone's 
rooting for Ide-kun.</i>

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:31.150
<i>It's people like him that 
are best suited for the pros.</i>

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:35.360
<i>But that's exactly why I want to beat him!</i>

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:39.660
<i>Going pro means beating players just like him!</i>

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:40.930
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.420
<i>He reacted fast!</i>

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>I have to nail it here,</i>

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.420
<i>or I'm not a man!</i>

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.190
<i>Huh? That cheering...</i>

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.500
<i>Is that from Ei-chan's court?</i>

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:11.440
That's Ide! When he sets out 
to do something, he does it!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.450
Ide-kun, you're awesome!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.910
Keep fighting too, Maruo-kun!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.470
Don't you dare lose, Ide-niichan!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.760
<i>That can't be helped on a flat serve.</i>

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.010
<i>Just don't get timid on my second one.</i>

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.490
Double fault. Love-30.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.710
No worries, Maruo!

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.720
Ide, now's your chance!

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.130
<i>What am I doing? A double fault 
at a crucial time like this?</i>

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.450
That's the third double fault today,

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:51.560
but it's the first one to 
happen on a critical point.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:54.560
They don't seem that far apart in skill,

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:57.240
so why does he keep getting 
into these tight situations?

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:01.240
I guess being cheered on has a 
bigger effect than we thought.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:04.540
When people are praised or feel joy,

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:08.540
the brain releases dopamine, 
which allows them to feel pleasure.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.470
When that happens, they're motivated by 
the desire to feel that pleasure again,

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:18.550
which can improve athletic ability 
and make them less prone to fatigue.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.090
Maruo, on the other hand,

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:24.560
is more likely to lose athletic ability 
and feel fatigue in this situation.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:31.630
Maruo has held out this long because his 
motivation to win this match was high,

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:36.660
but things like these take 
effect slowly, over time.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:49.080
<i>I didn't lose the first set 
because I was playing poorly.</i>

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.900
<i>It's because you're strong!</i>

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:56.170
<i>But I've beaten lots of guys 
who were stronger than me.</i>

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.930
<i>They say tennis is a lonely sport,</i>

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.690
<i>but I don't agree.</i>

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:09.270
<i>I've come this far because 
I had everyone's support.</i>

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:16.900
Yes!

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.900
Love-40.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.990
There it is! Ide's finally got break point!

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.300
Whoa!

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.790
<i>Don't get overwhelmed!</i>

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.900
<i>Ide-kun is taking advantage of the situation,</i>

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:30.690
<i>but that doesn't mean there's enough 
of a difference to let him break</i>

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:31.990
<i>my serve at love.</i>

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:36.300
<i>I have to face him with my pure, 
basic tennis, without freaking out!</i>

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:40.910
Yes!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.050
15-40.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.410
Pull through, Ei-chan!

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.560
30-40.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.220
Game: Ide. 5-3.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.160
Second set.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.170
Yes!

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.460
He finally broke!

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.910
This guy never lets his supporters down!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.290
Ei-chan... Break his serve right back!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.510
15-love.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:15.530
All right!

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:16.550
30-love.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:17.830
Yosshi!

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.550
Consecutive points!

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.930
Of course he has the edge. It's his serve!

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.330
That's it, Ide!

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.690
C-Come on, Maruo-kun!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.940
Oh, is that Maruo's girlfriend?

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.940
D-Don't lose now, Ei-chan!

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.050
<i>What now?</i>

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:40.200
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.700
<i>Ide-kun is able to turn everyone's 
belief in him into strength,</i>

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.950
<i>so even if he's playing stronger than usual,</i>

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.530
<i>it doesn't make sense that 
he can take it this far.</i>

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.980
<i>The cheering doesn't make it easy,</i>

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.770
<i>and it feels weird being in 
the middle of all this drama,</i>

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:57.230
<i>but I've done a good job of shrugging 
that off and playing my best.</i>

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:58.960
<i>So why?</i>

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.500
40-love.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.680
A service ace!

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.680
Win the next one in one shot, too!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:10.180
<i>He was probably aiming to hit 
that one right over the line.</i>

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:14.120
<i>This is the strength Ide-kun has 
that Nabae-kun talked about.</i>

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:17.460
<i>Just like Takuma-san and 
Araya-kun's quick reflexes,</i>

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.190
<i>it's a unique ability I don't have.</i>

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.960
<i>How do I overcome it?</i>

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:28.730
<i>That's not something I can see like 
the power of his shot, so I don't know!</i>

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.450
<i>Damn it! Don't get timid!</i>

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:37.980
Maruo Eiichiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:36.110
<i>Even if he wins this point, I'll only 
lose the second set, not the match.</i>

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:37.110
<i>So...</i>

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:40.770
<i>If everyone around is giving Ide-kun strength...</i>

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:46.610
<i>I need to hit a shot hard 
enough to quiet the cheering!</i>

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:47.970
Go!

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:58.700
<i>M-My sweat made the racket slip!</i>

00:20:58.700 --> 00:20:59.980
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:04.610
Second set winner: Ide. Score: 6-3.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.250
All right!

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:07.810
Way to go!

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.130
You're back on even footing 
with the sets at 1-all!

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:12.250
Show us what you've got 
again in the final set!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:16.460
<i>Damn! Why did this happen 
at such a crucial time?</i>

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:20.070
S-Sorry, could I get the ball back?

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:24.510
<i>Huh? Nabae-kun?</i>

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.290
Hey, isn't that Nabae?

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:30.480
The first seed is here to watch?

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.020
<i>How long has he been here?</i>

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:36.090
<i>He's holding a laptop. 
Does that mean he's scouting?</i>

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:42.780
<i>How does this match appear to Nabae-kun?</i>

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.110
<i>He's the one who said that victory goes 
to the swiftest with Ide-kun.</i>

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:50.860
<i>So even though the first 
set went well for me,</i>

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:53.290
<i>it probably looks like I'm being 
overwhelmed by the drama</i>

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.490
<i>of Ide-kun winning in tight situations.</i>

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:00.540
<i>No, more than "looks like." 
I </i>am<i> being overwhelmed.</i>

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:03.930
<i>The pressure got to me!</i>

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:16.100
<i>Even if I ignore pressure, what do 
I do if my body starts to feel it?</i>

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:25.930
<i>What can I do to win?</i>

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:31.130
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:24.980
Next Time

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:03.940
The more people expect from me, 
the stronger I become!

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:07.330
I'm going to use this strength 
I have to make everyone smile!

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:11.500
If I want to be freed from pressure 
and face him purely on our tennis,

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.880
I have to rise above the pressure.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.390
I need to face the things I've 
been averting my eyes from,

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:19.140
and otherwise, look only at Ide-kun as always,

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:20.270
and face him head-on!

00:24:20.550 --> 00:24:22.290
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.980
Visualize the Pressure

00:24:22.290 --> 00:24:23.930
"Visualize the Pressure."

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:31.000
End
